Whacking monsters with potions of paralysis does not check monster
magic resistance. Just try it with the Wizard.

Level drain is a bit more complicated: The drain life spell's level
drain effect does take into account monster magic resistance, while
level draining artifacts don't. Again, just wiz-mode test it with
Rodney.

If you want a complete list of things monster magic resistance
protects against, you will likely have to grep the source. Just two
pitfalls: player style magic resistance from gray dragon scale mail
protects against less things than innate resistance. Secondly, the
source does not always handle the same "attack" the same way in
different code paths. For example, conflict can generally be resisted,
always as ring-class even if from the Sceptre of Might, but there is
no resistance check in a lot of places: if pets will attack quest
leaders/guardians, if remote spellcasters will summon nasties etc.


